A base short of 13/13 means the INSTRUMENT is broken, and no variant score means anything (the rule that caught the
first version's run 1).  A floor variant (M2_len8, KILLLEN8, vc, vc_ne0..3, vf) scoring 13/13 is a floor breach of THIS
diff and blocks the commit.

================================================================ THE FOUR PRE-TABLE CHECKS
SIBLING PARITY -- the four cells are one machinery at four lanes: same a3 (16), same k (0), same string, one register
  each, preset != WANT at every cell.  The one asymmetry is the register KIND: the MSR reads back OR 0xb0, so its preset
  is written 0x00 and read 0xb0, and its WANT is s[2] | 0xb0; the xform is applied to BOTH sides, so the row compares
  like with like.  No arm is de-fatalised by this diff (detector-only), so no completion-event parity is owed.
CLAIM -> ROW -- the contract's DESIGNED TO CATCH sentence maps to rows: the guard and write-arm-conjunct forms -> all
  four getenv rows (M2_len8, KILLLEN8); a lane-conditioned form -> that lane's getenv row (vc, vc_ne0..3); a wrong lane
  byte -> the lane 1-3 getenv rows (vf; lane 0 cannot see it, since s[0] is the lane-0 byte).  Disclosures (i)-(viii)
  claim NO row, each with its warrant in the header.  The `live' rows claim a round-trip control only (#530 F7).
GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the guarded write arm reads `data[ofs]' (ofs = (relative_addr & 3) % len) and forwards to
  LCA_ISA_BASE + relative_addr.  LANE (relative_addr & 3) flows into a body-read lvalue -> a floor axis -> rowed at all
  four values.  The port beyond the lane flows only into the forward address -> the parent's p_port10 class, disclosed.
  `len' is tested only against 0 -> width thresholds are disclosed (i).  The discarded bits a<4:0> -> lcaisasize (iii).
CHANNEL -- every getenv row: the register value after the GETENV.  Under a variant that declines, refuses or drops the
  wide store into the read arm, the register KEEPS ITS PRESET (preset != WANT at all four cells, checked above); under a
  misroute (vf) it gets s[0], which differs from WANT at lanes 1-3.  So the channel varies under every floor variant by
  construction.  The `live' rows vary under none of them BY DESIGN (a round-trip control); the `alive' rows vary only
  under a reinstated process-ending call, which also reds getenv (t4-style print missing) -- survive-only companions.
  *** CHECKING THE CHANNEL LINE, as the carrier asks the first applications to: every prediction above names the
  row that differs and why, BEFORE any run.  The table will say whether that held. ***
